> Oh!  Question:  is it possible to tin Death, Famine or Pestilence?  
> Cause . . . . that would be awesome . . . anyone know?
> 
Short answer: You can't. Longer answer: they revive if you try to do 
anything (pick up, eat, tin, teleport, ...) to their corpses if there is 
a free space on the level. Even though this can be prevented by confused 
?oCM or a few priests and archons (you will get the message "you feel 
less hassled" and the corpse will start to rot), there unfortunately is 
a catch in the tinning code ("War doesn't preserve its enemies") that 
still prevents tinning. But with enough "oLS at least they can be eaten, 
as shown by GeneralKupior in 2005.

